        {
          "id": 1,
          "title": "3 Tips to Sell Your Montreal Home This Fall",
          "content": "Fall is one of the best selling seasons in Montreal — buyers are serious and inventory tightens. Here are three things I tell every seller before we list: 1) Get a pre-listing inspection. It catches surprises before buyers do. 2) Stage the entryway. First impressions matter more than people realize. 3) Price honestly. Overpricing kills momentum in the first two weeks.",
          "image_url": null,
          "category": "Tips",
          "published": 1,
          "created_at": "2026-05-16T16:03:26.754Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-05-16T16:03:26.754Z"
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "title": "Plateau vs. Rosemont: Where Should You Buy?",
          "content": "Two of Montreal's most beloved neighborhoods, two very different vibes. The Plateau is dense, lively, and walkable — perfect if you want cafés on every corner. Rosemont is greener, quieter, and more family-friendly. Prices reflect that: Plateau condos run higher per square foot, but Rosemont offers more space for the dollar.",
          "image_url": null,
          "category": "Tips",
          "published": 1,
          "created_at": "2026-05-16T16:03:26.762Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-05-16T16:03:26.762Z"
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "title": "What's Really Happening in the Montreal Market",
          "content": "After two years of buyer fatigue, we're seeing a clear shift. Quality properties priced right are getting multiple offers again. The lesson? Don't chase the market down. Price it right, prepare it well, and let buyers do the work.",
          "image_url": null,
          "category": "Market Update",
          "published": 1,
          "created_at": "2026-05-16T16:03:26.766Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-05-16T16:03:26.766Z"
        }
      ]
    },
